# Squid dstdomain allowlist -- RUNTIME phase (narrow).
#
# This is the steady state the agents run under. Everything not listed here is
# refused by the proxy, and the agent user has no route to the internet except
# through the proxy. verify/test-egress.sh asserts both halves of that.
#
# Activate with:  sudo agent-egress runtime
# A leading dot matches subdomains. One entry per line.

# --- Models -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Argo, via argo-proxy on 127.0.0.1:44497.
apps.inside.anl.gov

# --- Local fallback model ---------------------------------------------------
# DGX Spark vLLM endpoint over Tailscale. UNVERIFIED -- see docs/failover.md.
spark-ts

# --- Chat channels ----------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram is part of the base system, so the domain is allowed here. Note
# what this does and does not mean: the agents can *reach* Telegram, but no
# channel is enabled until a human turns one on. spec/pi-target-state.md
# requires Pi to configure channels disabled and stop, and verify.sh asserts
# zero live channels. Reachability and being switched on are separate things.
api.telegram.org
